SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Production should be knowledge-based and job-creating in the year 1401 SH","publisher":"Iran Watch","publication_date":"2022-03-20","url":"https://www.iranwatch.org/library/governments/iran/supreme-leader/production-should-be-knowledge-based-job-creating-year-1401-sh","claim":"Khamenei set the 2022 year slogan around production that is knowledge-based and job-creating, said past emphasis on production had produced good results, and urged officials to turn the slogan into real policy rather than decoration.","locator":"lines 244-251","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct reproduction of the Supreme Leader's Nowruz message with dated, attributable text and clear policy language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Khamenei statement; strong attribution for program identification and priorities.","contrary_evidence":["This is a program statement, not proof of execution.","It still relies on official self-report for the claimed prior-year success."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's Budget: Security and Order Gets Six Times More Funding than Water Resources","publisher":"Iran Open Data","publication_date":"2022-03-15","url":"https://iranopendata.org/en/article/iran-s-budget-security-and-order-gets-six-times-more-funding-than-water-resources/","claim":"Iran's 2022 budget bill allocated more than 54.8 trillion tomans for public order and security, a 14 percent increase, and the Shahid Ebrahimi security-infrastructure program rose about 386 percent year over year.","locator":"lines 30-31","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Quantified budget analysis with a clear 2022 fiscal claim, though it is an interpretive policy analysis rather than an official budget PDF.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Structural but relevant: this reflects ruling-network priorities under Khamenei's authority, not a personal instruction from him.","contrary_evidence":["It shows security prioritization, not whether the spending was efficient or effective.","The article is advocacy-adjacent analysis, so it needs corroboration."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"As nuclear talks resume, Iran's oil exports increase","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-02-10","url":"https://www.euronews.com/next/2022/02/10/iran-oil","claim":"Iranian oil exports rose above 1 million barrels per day for the first time in almost three years, showing the regime could sustain significant sanctioned oil flows to China despite U.S. pressure.","locator":"lines 659-661","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with precise quantified export estimates from tanker-tracking firms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to 2022 output and early-year trajectory.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the result reflects regime policy and sanctions-evasion capacity under Khamenei's system, not a personal order in the article.","contrary_evidence":["Reuters notes the exports still depended on sanction evasion and did not prove a durable policy solution.","The figure is an estimate, not an official Iranian statistic."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iranian oil exports end 2022 at a high, despite no nuclear deal","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2023-01-15","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/iranian-oil-exports-end-2022-at-a-high-despite-no-nuclear-deal-2980516","claim":"Iran's crude exports in December 2022 averaged 1.137 million barrels per day, the highest 2022 figure reported by SVB International, and exports had hit the highest since 2019 on some estimates.","locator":"lines 423-425","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with a concrete year-end estimate from an industry tracker and explicit comparison to prior years.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective but directly about the end of 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: it reflects the outcome of sanctions-resistance policy under Khamenei's regime rather than an individual command document.","contrary_evidence":["The source attributes part of the rise to market conditions and sanctions enforcement gaps, not just Iranian competence.","It remains an estimate rather than a state-released figure."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran appoints new central bank chief","publisher":"Reuters via Anews","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.anews.com.tr/middle-east/2022/12/29/iran-appoints-new-central-bank-chief","claim":"Iran appointed Mohammad Reza Farzin as central bank chief; the report noted his Bank Melli background and said the appointment came amid a record-low rial and inflation around 50 percent.","locator":"lines 58-60","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with a concrete appointment and contemporaneous macroeconomic context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Structural but relevant: the appointment reflects regime response and personnel choice under Khamenei's system, not a direct Khamenei quote.","contrary_evidence":["This shows adaptation, but in response to failure rather than clear success.","The report does not prove the new appointee improved outcomes by year-end."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran's judiciary says it will deal firmly with protesters","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/09/iran-women-judiciary","claim":"Iran's judiciary said courts would deal firmly with protesters, and the report said more than 1,000 people had been indicted in Tehran Province alone in connection with the unrest.","locator":"lines 653-660","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with specific numbers and contemporaneous protest-response details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the judiciary is part of the Khamenei-led regime's enforcement apparatus.","contrary_evidence":["This shows coercive control more than administrative competence in a policy sense.","It does not show whether the response resolved the underlying unrest."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran: Declaration by the High Representative on Behalf of the E.U.","publisher":"Iran Watch / European Union","publication_date":"2022-09-25","url":"https://www.iranwatch.org/library/multilateral-organizations/european-union/iran-declaration-high-representative-behalf-eu","claim":"The EU said Iranian authorities severely restricted internet access and blocked instant messaging platforms during the protests, which it said violated freedom of expression and should be stopped immediately.","locator":"lines 215-217","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official EU declaration with direct, dated attribution of the internet restrictions and an explicit description of the harm.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Structural but material: the action was by Iranian authorities under Khamenei's system, not a direct personal order in the document.","contrary_evidence":["The source condemns the action rather than evaluating whether it helped the regime maintain control.","It does not establish a direct link to a named individual beyond the authorities."],"lenses":["8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Iran’s Morality Police and Senior Security Officials for Violence Against Protesters and the Death of Mahsa Amini","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0994","claim":"OFAC designated Iran's Morality Police and seven senior security officials, saying these bodies routinely used violence to suppress protesters and other civil-society groups and were responsible for Amini's death and the crackdown.","locator":"lines 222-225 and 232-244","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary U.S. sanctions notice with concrete names, organizational roles, and detailed rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the named security organs are part of the regime Khamenei oversees; the document does not prove a direct personal command from him.","contrary_evidence":["This is an adversarial sanctions finding, so the language is not neutral.","It proves coercive implementation more clearly than strategic planning competence."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Iran acknowledges drone shipments to Russia before war, Kyiv says Tehran is lying","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-05","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/iran-acknowledges-drone-shipments-to-russia-before-war-kyiv-says-tehran-is-lying-2933668","claim":"Iran acknowledged it had supplied Moscow with drones before the war in Ukraine, and the report said Russia had used them to attack power stations and civilian infrastructure.","locator":"lines 421-427","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with explicit acknowledgment and direct linkage to battlefield use.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, with a near-term retrospective statement.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: this reflects a regime-level foreign-policy and military-support decision under Khamenei's umbrella.","contrary_evidence":["Iran said the drones were sent before the war, so the precise timing is contested.","The article does not identify Khamenei personally as the decision-maker."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. targets supply of Iranian drones to Russia in new sanctions","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-15","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/world-news/us-targets-production-transfer-of-iranian-drones-to-russia-in-new-sanctions-2828452","claim":"The United States said companies and people were involved in the production or transfer of Iranian drones used by Russia, and it identified the Shahed Aviation Industries Research Center as subordinate to the IRGC Aerospace Force.","locator":"lines 422-430 and 438-440","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with named entities, clear sanctions rationale, and specific organizational attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the entities are part of the Khamenei-led security network, though not a direct personal order in the report.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports U.S. sanctions allegations rather than an internal Iranian admission.","It measures foreign-policy execution, not domestic governance competence."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.4","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. adds Iran cargo planes flying to Russia to export violation list","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-19","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/us-adds-cargo-planes-operated-by-iranian-airlines-flying-to-russia-to-export-violation-list-2894909","claim":"The U.S. Commerce Department said three Iranian cargo planes serving Russia were transporting goods, including electronics, to Russia in apparent violation of export controls, and that Iran had publicly announced plans to expand aviation cooperation with Russia.","locator":"lines 409-414","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire based on a U.S. Commerce Department statement and commercially available tracking data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: it reflects a regime-linked aviation/logistics network under Khamenei's broader authority.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying data are indirect and not a direct Iranian confession.","The activity is relevant to influence and sanctions evasion, not to broad domestic effectiveness."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Britain sanctions Iran over supply of drones to Russia","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/20/ukraine-crisis-britain-iran","claim":"Britain sanctioned three Iranian military figures and a defense manufacturer for supplying Russia with drones to attack civilian and infrastructure targets in Ukraine, saying the individuals were personally responsible for the provision.","locator":"lines 606-611","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire with specific sanctioning of named individuals and a clear statement of personal responsibility.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the sanctioned officers belong to the Khamenei-aligned security apparatus, though the article does not prove a direct personal order.","contrary_evidence":["This is adversarial sanctions evidence rather than neutral monitoring.","It demonstrates military-influence execution more than civilian policy competence."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.4","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across Khamenei speeches, budget and macroeconomic reporting, Reuters wires and mirrors, Iran Watch reproductions, EU/U.S. sanctions notices, and Iran-focused analysis. I retained 16 reused evidence items and 10 newly accepted source-claim units above, then rejected or deprioritized:
- Duplicate Reuters mirror copies that repeated the same claim without adding a new material fact.
- Purely moral or human-rights items that fit 3B/4B better unless they also showed regime mobilization, control, or policy implementation.
- Out-of-period items that were useful background but not necessary once a target-year analogue existed.
- Generic country-capacity indicators that did not establish Khamenei's revealed program or ruler-attributable implementation.
- Sources that were too vague on attribution, such as broad commentary on Iranian politics without a concrete link to the leader's program, appointments, budget, or enforcement machinery.
- Repetitions of the same protest-censorship story from multiple outlets when one Reuters wire plus an official EU/Treasury notice already established the fact pattern.

**Remaining gaps**
- The dossier still lacks a direct internal document showing Khamenei personally ordering specific 2022 appointments, budget reallocations, or operational directives; some of the strongest evidence is inferred through his formal authority and the regime machinery he controls.
- Economic execution is mixed: there is clear program language and some sanctions-evasion/oil-export success, but the year also saw record-low rial, high inflation, and significant welfare pressure. More granular evidence on whether Khamenei's preferred economic program actually improved household conditions would help.
- I still have limited direct evidence on adaptation quality beyond the central-bank appointment and the move to intensify security spending. A clearer 2022 record of replace-or-correct behavior would strengthen 8B.8.
- If you want a tighter dossier, the next most useful search would be for official budget execution data, Central Bank/IRNA records on policy changes after the rial collapse, and additional primary documents on Khamenei-linked appointments or operational directives in the IRGC, judiciary, or economic network.
